  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">BRA480_Pastoral Social</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Brazilian National Bishop&apos;s Conference (CNBB) Comission aims at strengthening and integrating the work of the different thematic &quot;Pastorais Sociais&quot; through the Annual National Fraternity Campaign and the IV Brazilian Social Week, holding more than 250 events in the whole of the country throught the year.

This project is part of the Economic Justice Programme, a partnership between CAFOD and 4 church-based organisations, whose goal is to achieve greater economic justice in Brazil by addressing the key development issues of debt, trade, governance and human rights with a focus on awareness-raising, participation, social mobilisation and advocacy.

The project is: (1) publicizing the Economic Justice Programme&apos;s theme &quot;debt, social rights and social security system reform&quot; in all different &quot;Pastorais Sociais&quot;; (2) training the clergy on the protection of social rights in the 17 Regional Meetings of CNBB; (3) advocating for CNBB to become actively engaged in lobbying the government in defense of social rights; (4) Monitoring the government&apos;s actions that affect social rights and informing the CNBB of the information collected; (5) strengthening the partnership between the Church in Brazil and other church-based organisations and social movements.</narrative>
  </description>
